Dugout – Comprehensive QA, Product & Security Review

Executive Summary
The invite/join/roster feature set is functionally sound at its core — the happy paths work, errors are caught, and Row Level Security is relied upon for authorization. However, the system has a cluster of UX gaps, security concerns, and architectural weaknesses that make it not production-ready in its current state. The most critical issues center around: (1) the join code granting unrestricted parent role to anyone with the link, (2) no post-auth redirect for the invite flow when a user signs up fresh, (3) the acceptInvite having a TOCTOU race condition, (4) expected members having no edit capability or matching mechanism, and (5) zero automated test coverage.
Overall Production Readiness Score: 4 / 10

